<title>SPAIN: Spain ICO to issue $2 bln in EMTN programme.</title>
<headline>Spain ICO to issue $2 bln in EMTN programme.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish official credit agency Instituto de Credito Oficial (ICO) said on Thursday that it has signed an agreement to issue up to $2 billion in Euro Medium Term Notes (EMTN) programme, said arranger Goldman Sachs.</p>
<p>The note added that the multi-currency programme has no deadline and might be renewed on a yearly basis. The paper can be issued in maturities ranging from one month to 30 years.</p>
<p>The note added that ICO issues are guaranteed by the Spanish State.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
